    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d212">

                <pb facs="0409" n="347" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg347"/>

                <head>No. 207.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Edward Thornton to Mr.
                    Evarts</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-03-06"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 6, 1878</date>.
                        (Received March 7.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your note of the 20th
                    ultimo, I have the honor to inclose copy of a dispatch, and of its inclosure,
                    which I have received from the governor-general of Canada, conveying the assent
                    of the Canadian Government to the understanding that the provisional arrangement
                    in regard to the Alaska boundary shall not be held to affect the treaty rights
                    of either party.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>EDWD. THORNTON.</signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d212-a1.xml" xpointer="d212-a1"/>
